  "final": "Done. Change summary:\n\n**`src/repository.py`**\n- `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` now selects only rows where `id=? AND tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`, with all values passed as bound parameters. Returns `None` when no row matches (whether missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner, or deleted).\n- `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` now filters on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id`, with bound parameters, returning the same decoded `{id, title, body}` dictionaries (no deletion metadata).\n- `decode` and `initialize` unchanged; result field shape unchanged.\n\n**`src/service.py`**\n- `get_document` and `list_documents` now forward `tenant` and `owner` to the repository so enforcement lives in the query.\n\n**`checks/security.py`** (new)\n- Covers live/missing/cross-tenant/cross-owner/deleted lookups, list filtering and id ordering, empty results, quote-containing tenant/owner names (bound parameters, no injection), and absence of deletion metadata in results.\n\nVerification: `python3 checks/public.py` passes, `python3 checks/security.py` passes, and all files compile cleanly.",
